{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Command Aaron.</b> צַו is nothing but an expression of urging, for immediate observance and for the generations. Rabbi Shimon said: Scripture needs to urge all the more in a matter that involves monetary loss (Sifra)." "<b>This is the law of the burnt-offering, etc.</b> This matter comes to teach about the burning of fats and limbs — that it is valid all night. And to teach about the disqualified offerings: which, if they went up, must come down, and which, if they went up, do not come down. For every 'תּוֹרָה' comes to include — to say: one law for all that go up, even disqualified ones, that if they went up they do not come down (ibid.)." "<b>It is the burnt-offering.</b> To exclude the one that mounted and the one that was mounted and their like, which were not disqualified for the sacred service — for they were disqualified before they entered the courtyard (ibid. 8)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:10.103948070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}